# Export: PDF + CSV + Excel (AsanPay)

## Rule

Jahan bhi user **report / register / ledger / earnings / statement** download kare, export control **teen formats** offer kare:

1. **PDF** — branded print letterhead (`openBrandedPdf`) → browser “Save as PDF”
2. **Excel** — branded `.xls` (`downloadBrandedExcel`)
3. **CSV** — plain UTF-8 BOM CSV (imports / CA tools)

**Forbidden**
- Lone “Download Excel” / “Export CSV” / “Download” that only does one format
- “CSV export coming soon” stubs when a table is already on screen
- New export UIs that skip PDF or Excel

## UI

- Trigger label: **Export** (chevron dropdown)
- Menu order: **PDF → Excel → CSV**
- Empty data: disable trigger + clear toast (`Nothing to export…` / field-specific)
- English labels only

### Components

| Surface | Use |
|---------|-----|
| Agent web | `apps/agent-portal/components/ui/ExportMenu.tsx` + `lib/brandedExport.ts` |
| Admin web | Same pattern (`ExportMenu` in panel or shared) + `apps/admin-portal/lib/brandedExport.ts` |
| Mobile | Action sheet / menu: PDF · Excel · CSV (Share text/file). Prefer same three options on earnings, ledger, statements. |

## Implementation notes

- Build one `BrandedReport` (title, meta, summary, columns, rows) then call PDF + Excel from it; CSV from the same header/rows arrays.
- CSV helper: `downloadCsv` in agent `reportUtils` / admin utils — keep BOM `\uFEFF`.
- PDF needs pop-ups allowed — if `openBrandedPdf` returns false, toast: `Allow pop-ups for this site to export the PDF`
- Receipt PDFs for a **single txn** (API binary) are OK as one-off “PDF” actions — not the same as table Export menu.

## Done check

- [ ] Export control shows PDF, Excel, CSV
- [ ] All three produce usable files for the current filter range
- [ ] Web + mobile parity when the screen exists on both
- [ ] No Excel-only / CSV-only leftover label on that screen
